From f178d1f1f3b6b863e7f506dd6b2a78f41fe6c703 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:43:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use the released OpenSSL Bazel source-header fix

Select OpenSSL 3.5.5.bcr.1, whose Bazel integration includes PR #56,
instead of maintaining a downstream source-header workaround. Retain
Bazel dependency validation and generated platform configuration.
Adapt the existing LLVM 23 library and CLI backports to the selected
source formatting without changing their behavior.

Base: rust-v0.162.1 (092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d),
with native warning policy, LLVM 23, and OpenSSL warning backports.
Red: uncached unsandboxed compilation of 3.5.4.bcr.0 rejects the
shadowing opensslconf.h source header. 3.5.5.bcr.1 without the warning
backports rejects unused CLI globals under LLVM 23.
Green: the configuration-header and TLS/provider tests pass, and the
CLI version/help probe builds and runs with 2995 local actions and
both action and disk caches disabled. Native Windows acceptance is
separate. Evidence: openssl-module-upgrade-355bcr1-adapted.log.

Upstream: https://github.com/raccoons-build/bazel-openssl-cc/pull/56
---
 MODULE.bazel                                  |   2 +-
 patches/openssl_unused_globals.patch          | 162 ++++++++++--------
 tools/build-warnings/openssl/BUILD.bazel      |   7 +
 .../openssl/configuration_header_test.c       |   6 +
 4 files changed, 106 insertions(+), 71 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tools/build-warnings/openssl/configuration_header_test.c

diff --git a/MODULE.bazel b/MODULE.bazel
index c08937b78..ba304f40e 100644
--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -487,7 +487,7 @@ crate.annotation(
     deps = ["@xz//:lzma"],
 )

-bazel_dep(name = "openssl", version = "3.5.4.bcr.0")
+bazel_dep(name = "openssl", version = "3.5.5.bcr.1")
 single_version_override(
     module_name = "openssl",
     patch_strip = 1,
